00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:05.510
five additional episodes, we had five completed scripts.
额外的五集时，我们已经完成了五个剧本。

340
00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.170
And then they decided which one they were going to shoot.
然后他们才决定先拍哪一集。

341
00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.450
They didn't come out weekly.
它们不是每周播出一集那样写出来的。

342
00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.970
They did it collectively before we started the season.
是在我们开始拍摄这一季之前集体完成的。

343
00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:12.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

344
00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.870
Which, I guess that takes some of the pressure off.
我想这确实减轻了一些压力。

345
00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:16.970
It would.
确实会。

346
00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:17.490
Yeah.
是啊。

347
00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.470
And I have another fast fact.
我还有一个快讯事实。

348
00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:19.830
All right.
好吧。

349
00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:24.290
You do your fast facts because I've got some delicious note cards waiting for you.
你先说你的快讯事实吧，因为我这儿还有些精彩的笔记卡片等着你呢。

350
00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:24.750
All right.
好的。

351
00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.450
Some Kinsey tidbits over here.
这里有一些关于金赛的趣闻。

352
00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.730
I enjoy digesting your note cards.
我很喜欢消化你的笔记卡片。

353
00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:29.390
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

354
00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.130
Digest this first, though.
不过先消化一下这个。

355
00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:31.630
What?
什么？

356
00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:35.730
People, a lot of people want to know, where did the idea for this episode come from?
大家，很多人都想知道，这一集的灵感是从哪儿来的？

357
00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:41.230
This episode is based on the real-life experience of our writer's assistant, Tom.
这一集是基于我们编剧助理汤姆的真实经历改编的。

358
00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:45.410
So when they were in that writer's room, they throw out ideas for episodes.
当时他们在编剧室里，大家都在为剧集出谋划策。

359
00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.970
And Tom told this story about how when he was in college, he took a class.
汤姆讲了他在大学时上过的一门课。

360
00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:55.010
And in the class, they did this exercise where they had to put note cards on their heads
课上他们做了一个练习，每个人都要在头上贴一张笔记卡片，

361
00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.670
that said different ethnicities.
上面写着不同的种族。

362
00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.390
And then they had to go around and regard one another as that ethnicity.
然后他们必须走动起来，以那个种族的身份去对待彼此。

363
00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:01.490
Where did he go to school?
他是在哪儿上的学？

364
00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.110
Using stereotypes.
利用刻板印象。

365
00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.560
Where did he?
他是在哪儿上的？

366
00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:06.120
Don't know.
不知道。

367
00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:06.940
Holy moly.
天哪。

368
00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.440
But that happened.
但这确实发生过。

369
00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.100
Okay.
好吧。

370
00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.660
So let that sink in.
所以，好好消化一下这个事实吧。

371
00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.160
Yeah.
是啊。

372
00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:12.940
That happened to people.
这种事真的在人们身上发生过。

373
00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.260
Well, here's the thing I feel like about the show.
嗯，关于这部剧，我感觉是这样的。

374
00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:16.520
And listen, you guys watch it.
听着，你们都看过这部剧。

375
00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:16.920
You know.
你们懂的。

376
00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.280
There's a lot that happens that you're like, oh, yeah, something like that kind of happened
剧里发生了很多事，你会觉得，哦，是啊，类似的事情

377
00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:20.780
at my job.
在我的工作中也发生过。

378
00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:21.360
Yeah.
没错。

379
00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:28.180
I mean, when I worked at 1-800-DENTIS, we had to go to these human resources meetings
我是说，我在1-800-DENTIS工作时，我们必须参加那些人力资源会议，

380
00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:31.340
and they would act out skits for us about inappropriate behavior.
他们会为我们表演关于不当行为的小品。

381
00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.780
Well, you know what?
嗯，你知道吗？

382
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:37.360
Remember, we used to have to sit through those sexual harassment seminars on the office.
记得吗，我们以前在《办公室》剧组也得参加那些性骚扰研讨会。

383
00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:37.580
Yeah.
是啊。

384
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.180
The whole cast and crew would gather in the warehouse.
全体演职人员都要聚集在仓库里。

385
00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.260
And once a year, we had to get-
每年一次，我们必须参加——

386
00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.400
And the ABC made us do it.
而且是ABC电视台强迫我们做的。

387
00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:43.740
Yeah.
没错。

388
00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.400
Made us do sexual harassment training.
强迫我们进行性骚扰培训。

389
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.820
And then we signed papers saying we'd all behave appropriately at work.
然后我们还要签署文件，承诺在工作中表现得体。

390
00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.960
But do you remember what happened like in season four or five?
但你还记得第四季还是第五季发生的事吗？

391
00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.900
The video package that they showed us-
他们给我们放的视频片段——

392
00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:55.820
Was our show.
就是我们的剧。

393
00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:56.100
Was-
是——

394
00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:56.800
Of what not to do.
关于什么是不该做的。

395
00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:57.220
Yes.
是的。

396
00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:57.520
Yeah.
没错。

397
00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.880
Clips from the office.
《办公室》里的片段。

398
00:15:59.260 --> 00:15:59.400
Yeah.
是啊。

399
00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:03.800
We were sitting there watching clips of our show as examples of ways not to behave in
我们坐在那儿看着自己剧里的片段，作为职场中

400
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.200
a workplace.
不当行为的负面教材。

401
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:07.340
I've had actually a lot of people tell me that, that it comes up in different ways
其实很多人都跟我说过，这件事以各种不同的方式被提起，

402
00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:11.600
that they're in their- either college or work that our show is like, what not to do.
无论是在大学还是工作中，他们都说我们的剧就像是“反面教材”。

403
00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:12.600
All right.
好吧。

404
00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.280
I've got one more fast fact.
我还有一个快速小知识。

405
00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:15.960
And I also have a fan question.
我还有一个粉丝提问。

406
00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.140
Well, okay, good.
嗯，好的，不错。

407
00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.740
Because then I have some Kinsey tidbits.
因为我还有一些关于金赛的趣闻。

408
00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:19.300
Very good.
非常好。

409
00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.360
What would you like first?
你想先听哪个？

410
00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.220
The fast fact or the fan question?
快速小知识还是粉丝提问？

411
00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.560
Jenna, what is happening?
珍娜，你怎么了？

412
00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:24.780
Are you going out of order?
你是不按顺序来吗？

413
00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:25.620
Who are you?
你是谁啊？

414
00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.220
You're right.
你说得对。

415
00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:26.960
What am I saying?
我在说什么呢？

416
00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.460
I want the fast fact.
我想听快速小知识。

417
00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.040
Of course.
当然。

418
00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.400
Finish fast facts.
先把快速小知识讲完。

419
00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.740
And then go to fan questions.
然后再进行粉丝提问。

420
00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:32.520
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

421
00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.280
I'm feeling very loosey-goosey today, obviously.
显然我今天状态有点太松散了。

422
00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:35.900
All right.
好吧。

423
00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:36.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

424
00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.680
Final fast fact.
最后一个快速小知识。

425
00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.960
In this episode, we introduce two new characters.
在这一集中，我们引入了两个新角色。

426
00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.260
Yes, we do.
没错。

427
00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:49.860
Toby Flindersen and Kelly Kapoor, played by two more members of our writing staff, Paul Lieberstein
托比·弗林德森和凯莉·卡普尔，由我们编剧团队的另外两位成员保罗·利伯斯坦

428
00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.060
and Mindy Kaling.
和敏迪·卡灵饰演。

429
00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:51.640
Yes.
是的。

430
00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.560
I do have to say, I love the name Toby Flindersen.
我不得不说，我超爱“托比·弗林德森”这个名字。

431
00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:59.380
I love when a character's name sort of describes the character.
我喜欢那种名字本身就能体现角色特质的感觉。

432
00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:03.520
But, like, the name Toby Flindersen, like, when you see Paul on screen as Toby, you're
但是像“托比·弗林德森”这个名字，当你看到保罗在屏幕上饰演托比时，你会觉得

433
00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.280
like, oh, of course that's Toby Flindersen.
噢，当然，他就是托比·弗林德森。

434
00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:06.000
That's who that is.
他就是那个人。

435
00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:06.880
Absolutely perfect.
简直太完美了。

436
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:11.360
A lot of people ask, why were so many writers actors on the show?
很多人问，为什么剧里有那么多编剧同时也是演员？

437
00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.620
And that was Greg Daniels.
那是格雷格·丹尼尔斯的主意。

438
00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:19.440
Greg believed that it would be a good idea for writers to have the experience of acting
格雷格认为让编剧有演戏的经验是个好主意，

439
00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:25.520
because it would give them a deeper appreciation of what an actor does, which I have to say is
因为这能让他们更深刻地理解演员的工作，我不得不说这真的

440
00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:32.540
so brilliant, and I think there are a lot of directors that I know go take acting classes
太聪明了，我知道很多导演都会去上表演课，

441
00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:37.800
just so they can better speak to actors and understand actors, and it completely worked
就是为了能更好地与演员沟通并理解演员，这在我们的剧里完全奏效了，

442
00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:42.920
on our show that the writers were immersed with us because they really got to not just
编剧们和我们打成一片，因为他们不仅真正

443
00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:47.720
understand our jobs, but they got to see us being our characters firsthand.
理解了我们的工作，还亲眼看到了我们如何塑造角色。

444
00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:52.780
They got to see our little improvisations that they would never see if they were just stuck
他们看到了我们那些即兴发挥，如果他们只是被困在

445
00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:57.900
up in the writer's room, and all of that ended up becoming a part of the show.
编剧室里，是永远看不到这些的，而所有这些最终都成为了剧集的一部分。

446
00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.280
I think it was so great.
我觉得这太棒了。

447
00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:03.640
It really made us a cohesive show between the two departments, sort of the writers,
这真的让我们两个部门之间形成了一个紧密的整体，也就是编剧和

448
00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.620
the actors, this creative partnership.
演员之间，这种创造性的伙伴关系。

449
00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:10.080
It always felt like a partnership to me and made me feel safe, like I could try things,
对我来说，这感觉一直是一种伙伴关系，让我感到很有安全感，觉得我可以尝试各种东西，

450
00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:10.360
you know?
你懂吗？

451
00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:10.720
Yes.
是的。

452
00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:14.180
But, you know, BJ and Mindy were really great performers.
但你知道，BJ和敏迪确实是非常出色的表演者。

453
00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.300
They were crossovers.
他们是跨界艺人。

454
00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.560
But Paul was not a performer.
但保罗并不是表演者。

455
00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.700
Paul had only just been a writer.
保罗一直以来都只是个编剧。

456
00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:23.840
So I know this was, like, a huge sort of, like, step out of his comfort zone.
所以我知道这对他来说，就像是迈出了舒适区的一大步。

457
00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:29.060
And I think he thought it was going to be just this one little line in this episode.
而且我想他当时以为这只是这一集里的一句小台词而已。

458
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:29.340
Right.
没错。

459
00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.940
Well, Jenna texted him this morning.
嗯，珍娜今天早上给他发了短信。

460
00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:31.340
I did.
是我发的。

461
00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.460
It was like, Paul, tell us the dish on how you became Toby.
内容大概是：保罗，跟我们说说你是怎么成为托比的内幕吧。

462
00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.440
And he just said, Greg kind of made me do it.
他只回了一句：是格雷格逼我演的。

463
00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.980
He said he remembered walking in one day, and it had been decided that he was going to play
他说他记得有一天走进办公室，就得知已经决定由他来扮演

464
00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.280
this role of Toby.
托比这个角色了。

465
00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.000
And he really thought it was just going to be this one line.
他当时真的以为就只有那一句台词。

466
00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:48.300
Right.
没错。

467
00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.420
He didn't think he was going to be a series regular.
他没想到自己会成为常驻演员。

468
00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:50.920
Right.
没错。

469
00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:51.200
No.
没有。

470
00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:53.880
He did not think it was going to grow into what it was.
他没想到这会发展成后来的样子。

471
00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:58.280
But Kevin Riley, who was the head of NBC at the time, saw this episode.
但当时NBC的负责人凯文·莱利看了这一集。

472
00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.220
He loved it.
他很喜欢。

473
00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:03.200
He loved the dynamic between Michael Scott and Toby Flunderson.
他很喜欢迈克尔·斯科特和托比·弗兰德森之间的化学反应。

474
00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.120
And he said, I want more of that.
于是他说，我想要更多这样的内容。

475
00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.100
I want more Toby.
我想要更多托比的戏份。

476
00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.840
And so then Paul officially became an actor on the show.
就这样，保罗正式成为了剧中的一名演员。

477
00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.380
Paul, who was not a performer and who was kind of a quiet person in real life,
保罗，一个本不是表演者，在现实生活中又有点安静的人，

478
00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.060
all of a sudden became a full-time actor and writer.
突然间变成了一名全职演员兼编剧。

479
00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:24.320
I think something we have to talk about, too, is the transformation of Kelly Kapoor.
我觉得我们还得聊聊凯莉·卡普尔的转变。

480
00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:30.260
A lot of fans wrote in asking about this, and I'm sure you've got a note card about it, Angela.
很多粉丝写信问过这件事，安吉拉，我肯定你准备了小卡片。

481
00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:31.020
I do.
没错。

482
00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:34.880
First of all, all my note cards today are green, and Jenna has already said they're whorish.
首先，我今天所有的卡片都是绿色的，珍娜已经说它们很“风骚”了。

483
00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:36.280
But whatever, Jenna.
但无所谓啦，珍娜。

484
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:40.540
So I have a note card that's just written, Kelly's outfit.
我这张卡片上只写了：凯莉的装扮。

485
00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:41.100
Yeah.
没错。

486
00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.340
Exclamation point.
后面还有个感叹号。

487
00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:44.120
Because this is hilarious.
因为这太搞笑了。

488
00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:50.140
Anyone that knows, Mindy, knows that after this episode, she was like, yeah, I'm not going to dress like that.
了解敏迪的人都知道，这一集之后，她就觉得：好吧，我才不要穿成那样。

489
00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:50.460
Okay?
好吗？

490
00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:54.240
Because she had on this sort of paisley blouse and those pants.
因为她当时穿了一件那种佩斯利花纹的衬衫，还有那条裤子。

491
00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.660
That went all the way up to her neck.
领口一直高到脖子那里。

492
00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.120
I know, and her hair up in like an updo, and it was just so funny to me.
我知道，她还梳了个发髻，这对我来说太搞笑了。

493
00:19:59.120 --> 00:19:59.740
Very fussy.
非常老气。

494
00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:03.140
Very fussy and sort of like just like buttoned up.
非常老气，而且看起来就是那种扣得严严实实的样子。

495
00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:08.740
And right after like this episode, I feel like she was like, yeah, I'm going to come in for a real wardrobe fitting,
我觉得就在这一集之后，她就想：好吧，我要去参加一次正式的服装试装，

496
00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:12.040
and we're going to change up the way Kelly Kapoor looks.
我们要改变凯莉·卡普尔的造型。

497
00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:17.140
I think when she realized, same as Paul, that this was going to be more than just a one-off,
我想当她和保罗一样意识到这不仅仅是一次客串，

498
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.860
that she would be appearing regularly on the show,
她会成为剧中的常驻角色时，

499
00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:25.040
not only did her wardrobe change, but the whole conceit of her character change.
不仅她的服装变了，她整个角色的设定也变了。

500
00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:29.300
And she started writing herself more into the character, the love of Beyonce,
她开始在角色中加入更多自己的影子，比如对碧昂丝的热爱，

501
00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:34.720
and, you know, the clothes, and the fashion show, fashion show, fashion show at lunch.
还有，你知道的，那些衣服，还有时装秀，午餐时的时装秀。

502
00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.280
That's all Mindy.
那全是敏迪的主意。

503
00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:37.520
The romance with BJ.
和BJ的那段恋情。

504
00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:38.760
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

505
00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:40.800
Correct.
对。

506
00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.280
All of those elements sort of weaved their way into the show,
所有这些元素都以某种方式融入了剧中，

507
00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.200
but it is true.
但这是真的。

508
00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.540
In this first incarnation of Kelly Kapoor, she is.
在凯莉·卡普尔最初的设定里，她确实是那样。

509
00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:49.620
Very different.
非常不同。

510
00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:52.880
Not the Kelly we eventually learned to love.
不是我们后来学会去爱的那位凯莉。

511
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:55.940
And I love the Kelly she became, though, because she was so fun,
但我很喜欢她后来变成的样子，因为她太有趣了，

512
00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:01.740
and just added so much like sort of like just sunshine to like whatever scene she was in.
而且给每一场戏都增添了许多阳光般的气息。

513
00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:03.660
I don't know how to say it, but like there was always –
我不知道该怎么形容，但总觉得——

514
00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:07.260
she was just all so bubbly and everything, and everyone else was so drab.
她总是那么活泼开朗，而其他人却显得那么沉闷。

515
00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:09.640
So I thought she added much-needed energy.
所以我认为她注入了急需的活力。

516
00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.200
She added literal color.
她带来了真正的色彩。

517
00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:11.580
Yeah, she did.
没错，确实如此。

518
00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.280
She was the only person who dressed literally colorfully.
她是唯一一个穿得色彩鲜艳的人。

519
00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.260
So do you want my fan question?
那么，你想听听粉丝提问吗？

520
00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:18.560
Do I?
我想吗？

521
00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:19.000
Okay.
好吧。

522
00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.640
Heather from Twitter asked –
推特上的希瑟问——

523
00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:22.180
Hi, Heather.
嗨，希瑟。

524
00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:22.780
Hi, Heather.
嗨，希瑟。

525
00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:24.200
Heather asked,
希瑟问，

526
00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.560
since it was only the second episode,
因为那才第二集，

527
00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.940
what was the atmosphere on set like filming?
拍摄时的片场氛围如何？

528
00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:31.760
And I thought that was a really good question
我觉得这是一个非常好的问题，

529
00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:37.400
because we shot Diversity Day about six months after we shot the pilot.
因为我们在拍完试播集大约六个月后才拍摄《多元日》。

530
00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:41.000
We took this really long break because we were waiting to find out
我们休息了很长一段时间，因为我们在等消息，

531
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.840
if we were going to get picked up or not.
看我们是否会被续订。

532
00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:48.800
And it was so thrilling to be reunited again.
能再次重聚真是太令人激动了。

533
00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:52.020
I remember when we were watching Diversity Day, people have asked me,
我记得当我们看《多元日》的时候，有人问我，

534
00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:53.340
when did you feel like you had a hit?
你是什么时候觉得这部剧会火的？

535
00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:56.260
And I said, it's the moment we were all in the room,
我说，就在我们所有人都在那个房间里，

536
00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:59.060
and we all had those note cards taped to our foreheads.
额头上都贴着那些卡片的那一刻。

537
00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:02.320
And I was just looking around at all of us,
我环顾四周看着大家，

538
00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:05.300
and Steve was being Michael, and he was being so hilarious.
史蒂夫正在演迈克尔，他演得太搞笑了。

539
00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:09.840
And I thought, oh, my God, if we can just get anyone to watch the show,
当时我就想，天哪，只要能让人看到这部剧，

540
00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:10.600
we're going to be a hit.
我们一定会火。

541
00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.940
If anyone sees it, it's so good.
只要有人看，它真的太棒了。

542
00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:18.400
And it really was in that moment, I was like, oh, wow, this is lightning in a bottle.
就在那一刻，我真的觉得，哇，这简直是千载难逢的杰作。

543
00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:20.600
Now, how do we get the world to watch it?
现在，我们要怎么让全世界都看到它呢？

544
00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:22.580
Aw, I love that, Ange.
噢，我喜欢这个，安吉。

545
00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:24.500
Listen, should we take a break?
听着，我们要不要休息一下？

546
00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:25.860
Yeah, let's take a break.
好，我们休息一下。

547
00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:27.700
I have lots of note cards.
我有很多卡片。

548
00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:28.160
Well, perfect.
太完美了。

549
00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:30.540
When we come back, we will really break down Diversity Day
回来后，我们将深入剖析《多元日》，

550
00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:32.840
and get into the scenes and tell you all our stories.
细聊剧中的场景，并告诉你们我们所有的故事。

551
00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.440
You say diversity.
你说多元化。

552
00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:36.160
I say diversity.
我说多元化。

553
00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:37.180
What?
什么？

554
00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:38.540
Yeah, it's just been bugging me.
是啊，这事一直困扰着我。

555
00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:38.920
But anyway.
不过话说回来。

556
00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:40.920
Okay, let's go to a break.
好了，我们休息一下。

557
00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:51.920
And we're back.
欢迎回来。

558
00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:52.500
Hello.
大家好。

559
00:22:53.020 --> 00:22:57.660
All right, so the Diversity Day episode starts with Michael explaining that today
好的，那么《多元化日》那一集开头，迈克尔解释说今天

560
00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:00.880
the office is having a mandatory diversity training.
办公室要进行强制性的多元化培训。

561
00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:01.480
Yes.
没错。

562
00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:06.320
We also learned that today is the day that Jim is going to make his biggest sale of the year.
我们还了解到，今天也是吉姆要完成他全年最大一笔销售的日子。

563
00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:09.000
He explains he only has to make one phone call,
他解释说他只需要打一个电话，

564
00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:11.920
and it amounts to 25% of his total sales for the year.
这笔交易就占了他全年总销售额的25%。

565
00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:16.120
But Dwight keeps making it impossible for him to make that call.
但德怀特一直让他无法拨出那个电话。

566
00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:20.340
And so the first way that Dwight makes it impossible for him to make this phone call
德怀特让他无法拨出这个电话的第一个手段

567
00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:23.500
is that he must shred paper at his desk.
就是让他必须在办公桌前碎纸。

568
00:23:23.640 --> 00:23:24.580
Oh, Dwight.
噢，德怀特。

569
00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:27.100
Which I always thought was funny because, you know,
我一直觉得这很有趣，因为你知道，

570
00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:30.360
Pam has that industrial-sized shredder behind her desk.
帕姆的办公桌后面有那台工业级的碎纸机。

571
00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:34.460
Pam has a shredder like the size of a Xerox machine behind her desk.
帕姆办公桌后面有一台像施乐复印机那么大的碎纸机。

572
00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:35.840
Which we never use.
我们从来不用。

573
00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:36.320
Never use.
从来不用。

574
00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:36.600
Ever.
一次都没用过。

575
00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:38.460
I never shredded a single thing in it.
我从来没往里面碎过任何东西。

576
00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:41.500
And it used to get in the way when the camera—
而且它以前总是挡路，当摄像机——

577
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:42.180
You had to move it.
你得把它挪开。

578
00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:46.100
And it was a big argument over whether or not they could move it.
关于能不能挪动它，还引发过一场大争论。

579
00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:48.400
Like, the integrity of the documentary crew,
就像是纪录片摄制组的完整性问题，

580
00:23:49.060 --> 00:23:52.400
would they have moved the industrial shredder or not?
他们到底该不该挪动那台工业碎纸机？

581
00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:55.160
And so I remember a day we were on set,
我记得有一次我们在片场，

582
00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:57.500
and they wanted to get this shot behind my desk.
他们想拍我办公桌后面的镜头。

583
00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.960
And they said, if we could just move the shredder,
他们说，如果我们能挪一下碎纸机，

584
00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:03.540
we could get the shot you're asking for.
就能拍到你们想要的镜头了。

585
00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:08.860
And it was like a 30-minute argument over whether or not they could move or not move the shredder.
结果为了能不能挪动碎纸机，我们争论了大概30分钟。

586
00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:09.120
Right.
没错。

587
00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:12.220
Because they didn't want to, like, ruin the integrity of the documentary look.
因为他们不想破坏纪录片风格的完整性。

588
00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:12.290
Yes.
是的。

589
00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:13.940
This was a big thing all the time.
这事儿一直是个大问题。

590
00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:17.380
They decided, you know, you can't move walls.
他们决定，你知道，墙不能动。

591
00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:18.220
You can't move windows.
窗户不能动。

592
00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.660
You can't move furniture.
家具不能动。

593
00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:24.260
They did agree you could move this one plant around, the ficus.
但他们同意你可以挪动这一盆植物，那棵榕树。

594
00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:25.440
You could move the ficus.
你可以挪动那棵榕树。

595
00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:29.440
They clearly agreed that you could move that conference table out and put chairs,
他们显然同意你可以把会议桌搬走换成椅子，

596
00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:31.380
and then all of a sudden the conference table would be back.
然后突然之间会议桌又会变回来。

597
00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:32.240
I've had—
我曾经——

598
00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:33.100
Where did the conference table go?
会议桌去哪儿了？

599
00:24:33.100 --> 00:24:34.020
Where did the conference table go?
会议桌去哪儿了？

600
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:34.700
I know.
我知道。

601
00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:38.400
I've had so many people write to me, like, on social media be like,
很多人在社交媒体上给我留言，问我，

602
00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:40.040
what happened with the conference table?
会议桌去哪儿了？

603
00:24:40.100 --> 00:24:41.220
It was there, and then it's gone.
它明明在那儿，然后就不见了。

604
00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:42.600
Where does the conference table go?
会议桌到底去哪儿了？

605
00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:46.660
And I told them, I said, you know what I would have loved at the end of one episode?
我告诉他们，我说，你们知道我多希望在某一集的结尾能看到什么吗？

606
00:24:46.660 --> 00:24:52.380
All it would take is one episode, and the whole nine seasons, if at the end credits,
只需要一集，哪怕九季里只有这一集，如果在片尾字幕的时候，

607
00:24:52.380 --> 00:24:58.560
it just showed, like, Kevin and, like, Jim breaking down the conference table and Dwight
能展示一下凯文和吉姆拆掉会议桌，还有德怀特，

608
00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:02.540
and, like, stacking it in some storage thing and then having to go get it and put it back together.
把它堆在某个储藏室里，然后还得去把它拿出来重新组装好。

609
00:25:02.580 --> 00:25:04.100
But just as the credits rolled.
就在片尾字幕滚动的时候。

610
00:25:04.300 --> 00:25:04.660
Yes.
没错。

611
00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:08.800
I would love to see them carrying the conference table down to the warehouse or something.
我真想看他们把会议桌搬到仓库或者什么地方去。

612
00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:08.970
Like, in pieces.
拆成碎片搬走。

613
00:25:08.970 --> 00:25:10.000
Because where is it?
因为它到底在哪儿呢？

614
00:25:10.180 --> 00:25:10.700
I don't know.
我不知道。

615
00:25:10.700 --> 00:25:12.240
There is nowhere for it to be.
它根本没地方放。

616
00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:12.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

617
00:25:12.860 --> 00:25:13.720
It is.
它就是在那儿。

618
00:25:13.820 --> 00:25:15.840
That is one of the great mysteries of the show.
那是这部剧最大的未解之谜之一。

619
00:25:15.960 --> 00:25:17.020
Where is the conference table?
会议桌到底在哪儿？

620
00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:20.300
Every time Michael was, like, conference room meeting, that they were like, ugh,
每次迈克尔说“会议室开会”时，他们都会叹气，

621
00:25:20.460 --> 00:25:22.100
because they knew they had to break down that table.
因为他们知道自己得去拆那张桌子。

622
00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:23.960
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

623
00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:27.040
Well, do you remember that shredding scene where Rain is shredding the paper?
对了，你还记得雷恩碎纸的那场戏吗？

624
00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:28.140
Yes.
记得。

625
00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:29.560
And so he's shredding paper.
当时他在碎纸。

626
00:25:29.700 --> 00:25:30.280
He's shredding paper.
他在碎纸。

627
00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:36.820
So then Rain notices that there's a special slot on his personal shredder for a credit card,
然后雷恩注意到他的个人碎纸机上有一个专门用来碎信用卡的插槽，

628
00:25:36.840 --> 00:25:38.100
and he kind of stopped the filming.
他当时停下了拍摄。

629
00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:42.280
And he said, guys, I think I should shred a credit card.
他说，伙计们，我觉得我应该碎一张信用卡。

630
00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:44.960
And we were thinking, well, okay.
我们当时想，好吧，行吧。

631
00:25:45.560 --> 00:25:48.260
And he said, no, there's a special slot for it.
他说，不，这里有个专门的插槽。

632
00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:48.580
I know.
我知道。

633
00:25:48.660 --> 00:25:49.960
And everyone was like, is it going to work?
大家都心想，这真的能行吗？

634
00:25:50.160 --> 00:25:52.280
And so he did it.
于是他就试了。

635
00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:52.900
He did it.
他真的试了。

636
00:25:53.040 --> 00:25:56.620
They got him, like, a fake, like, credit card kind of thing, the props department.
道具组给了他一张假的信用卡之类的东西。

637
00:25:56.840 --> 00:25:59.140
And he did it, but it almost broke that shredder.
他试了，但差点把碎纸机弄坏。

638
00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:00.380
It started going like, eee.
它开始发出那种“吱——”的声音。

639
00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:06.580
I remember sitting there and thinking, is it, you know, is it, what's happening?
我记得我当时坐在那儿想，这，你知道，这是怎么了？

640
00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:07.580
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

641
00:26:07.820 --> 00:26:09.000
But he was so determined.
但他当时太执着了。

642
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.920
I also think Rain is like a gadget person a little bit.
我觉得雷恩也有点像个电子产品发烧友。

643
00:26:11.960 --> 00:26:13.360
So he was like, oh, there's a thing on here.
所以他当时就觉得，哦，这上面有个功能。

644
00:26:13.500 --> 00:26:14.160
I need to do it.
我一定要试一下。

645
00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:15.960
Yeah, I need to work this part of the machine.
没错，我得把机器的这个功能用上。

646
00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:16.640
I need to do it.
我一定要试一下。

647
00:26:16.920 --> 00:26:18.380
Angela, would you like to do a card?
安吉拉，你想抽一张卡吗？

648
00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:19.680
I would, Jenna Fisher.
我想抽，珍娜·费舍。

649
00:26:20.260 --> 00:26:23.480
Okay, so this card applies to the opening shot of the whole episode.
好的，这张卡对应的是整集开头的镜头。

650
00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:26.960
There is a great establishing shot of the Homer Simpson doll.
有一个非常棒的荷马·辛普森玩偶的定场镜头。

651
00:26:27.280 --> 00:26:30.800
The camera is going past Phyllis's desk, and it's sitting right there.
摄像机经过菲利斯的办公桌时，它就放在那儿。

652
00:26:31.260 --> 00:26:36.220
And, you know, it just makes me smile because I know that Greg Daniels wrote on The Simpsons,
你知道，这让我会心一笑，因为我知道格雷格·丹尼尔斯曾为《辛普森一家》写过剧本，

653
00:26:36.300 --> 00:26:41.500
and this was his little, like, nod to, like, the first part of his career, right?
这是他对他职业生涯早期的一种致敬，对吧？

654
00:26:41.680 --> 00:26:41.960
Yes.
没错。

655
00:26:42.180 --> 00:26:44.020
And it sat there all nine years.
它在那里放了整整九年。

656
00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:44.520
It did.
确实。

657
00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:45.300
That Simpson doll.
那个辛普森玩偶。

658
00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:46.560
So I love that.
所以我很喜欢这一点。

659
00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:48.340
That's just, like, kind of a dorky moment.
这真是个有点呆萌的瞬间。

660
00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:50.400
You guys know I love the things in the background.
你们知道我喜欢背景里的那些小细节。

661
00:26:50.720 --> 00:26:53.360
Well, you know what he did for the main caSt.
好吧，你知道他为主要演员做了什么吗？

662
00:26:53.360 --> 00:26:54.000
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

663
00:26:54.260 --> 00:26:55.380
I do know this.
我是知道这件事的。

664
00:26:55.540 --> 00:26:56.140
You do know.
你确实知道。

665
00:26:56.280 --> 00:26:57.960
Are you saying I'm sorry because I didn't get one?
你是说我道歉是因为我没收到吗？

666
00:26:58.060 --> 00:26:58.340
Yeah.
是的。

667
00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:00.100
Because you're calling me not main cast?
因为你觉得我不是主要演员？

668
00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:02.940
We called you supporting caSt.
我们当时称你们为配角。

669
00:27:03.200 --> 00:27:03.900
Is this?
这是什么？

670
00:27:06.320 --> 00:27:07.540
As a gift.
作为礼物。

671
00:27:07.880 --> 00:27:11.620
You guys, the rest of us didn't become series regular until Booze Cruise.
伙计们，我们其他人直到《游轮派对》那集才成为常规演员。

672
00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:12.840
That's a story for later.
那是后话了。

673
00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:14.820
But in the beginning, the main—
但在最初，主要——

674
00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:16.040
There were just five of us.
当时只有我们五个。

675
00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:20.940
Well, there weren't just the five of you, but you were the five that were the, quote, series regulars.
嗯，其实不只是你们五个，但你们五个是所谓的“常规演员”。

676
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:21.480
That's right.
没错。

677
00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:24.220
There were just the five series regulars, I should say.
应该说，当时只有五个常规演员。

678
00:27:24.220 --> 00:27:27.160
And the rest of us were just trash in the corner.
而我们其他人只是角落里的垃圾。

679
00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:32.260
No, but we had to do a lot of extra stuff.
不，但我们当时确实做了很多额外的工作。

680
00:27:32.500 --> 00:27:33.900
You had to do press and whatnot.
你们得参加媒体宣传之类的活动。

681
00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:40.560
We had to do press, and we had to do these crazy photo shoots, and we did all this stuff as the show was launching.
我们得做宣传，还得拍那些疯狂的照片，在剧集刚开播时我们做了所有这些事。

682
00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:42.860
Listen, there is no debating.
听着，这没什么好争论的。

683
00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:46.360
You guys were the core main cast, and the rest of us filled out the picture.
你们是核心主演，而我们其他人只是填充了画面。

684
00:27:46.820 --> 00:27:50.900
And then it grew, and then the cast grew, and then we had all of these series regulars.
后来剧集发展了，演员阵容也扩大了，我们才有了这么多常规演员。

685
00:27:50.900 --> 00:27:58.760
But I'm going to give you a little shiitake sometimes.
但我有时还是会给你找点小麻烦。

686
00:27:59.160 --> 00:27:59.800
All right, listen.
好吧，听着。

687
00:28:00.120 --> 00:28:11.040
So as a gift, Greg had the illustrators over at The Simpsons turn us all into Simpson characters.
作为礼物，格雷格让《辛普森一家》的插画师把我们都画成了辛普森角色。

688
00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:11.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

689
00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:18.900
And it was me, John, Rain, and Steve huddled around a computer.
当时是我、约翰、雷恩和史蒂夫围在电脑前。

690
00:28:19.180 --> 00:28:21.700
Now that I'm saying it, I realize I think B.J.
现在说起来，我意识到我觉得B.J.

691
00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:23.300
Novak was left out of this photo.
诺瓦克好像没在那张照片里。

692
00:28:23.560 --> 00:28:24.120
Sorry, B.J.
抱歉，B.J.

693
00:28:25.480 --> 00:28:32.220
But we were Simpsonized, and he gave us these illustrations in like a frame.
但我们被“辛普森化”了，他把这些插画装在相框里送给了我们。

694
00:28:32.700 --> 00:28:33.800
It's really cool.
真的很酷。

695
00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:34.640
It's really cool.
真的很酷。

696
00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:35.700
It's in my living room.
它现在就在我的客厅里。

697
00:28:35.760 --> 00:28:38.060
It's like a treasured item from the show.
这是我从剧组得到的珍贵物品之一。

698
00:28:38.060 --> 00:28:39.100
Jenna is a Simpson.
珍娜是个辛普森角色了。

699
00:28:39.420 --> 00:28:41.460
I have a Simpson version of me.
我有一个辛普森版本的自己。

700
00:28:41.900 --> 00:28:42.340
All right.
好吧。

701
00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:47.600
I want to talk about Pam's free sell, and so does BNG Chris on Twitter.
我想聊聊帕姆的空当接龙，推特上的BNG Chris也想聊。

702
00:28:47.840 --> 00:28:49.720
Well, let's hear it, BNG Chris.
好吧，让我们听听BNG Chris怎么说。

703
00:28:50.020 --> 00:28:50.500
All right.
好的。

704
00:28:50.620 --> 00:28:53.640
He asked if we were actually good at free sell.
他问我们是不是真的擅长玩空当接龙。

705
00:28:54.720 --> 00:28:57.440
And the answer is, oh, yes, we were.
答案是，哦，是的，我们确实很擅长。

706
00:28:57.600 --> 00:28:58.700
You want to know why?
你想知道为什么吗？

707
00:28:58.900 --> 00:29:00.380
This is one of my note cards, too.
这也是我的笔记卡片之一。

708
00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:04.260
We didn't get Wi-Fi until July of 2006.
我们直到2006年7月才装上无线网。

709
00:29:04.260 --> 00:29:10.360
And it was such a big deal on our set that a memo went around, and I saved the memo.
当时这在片场可是件大事，甚至还发了备忘录，我把那份备忘录留了下来。

710
00:29:10.500 --> 00:29:15.920
It was because, to give you some context, we shot this episode in 2004.
为了让你了解背景，我们是在2004年拍摄这一集的。

711
00:29:16.460 --> 00:29:16.800
Yes.
没错。

712
00:29:16.960 --> 00:29:19.960
And so it wasn't until 2006 that we got internet.
所以直到2006年我们才有了互联网。

713
00:29:20.020 --> 00:29:22.020
So for the pilot, they were nothing.
所以拍试播集的时候，它们什么都不是。

714
00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:24.040
They were literally like pieces of plastic.
它们简直就是塑料片。

715
00:29:24.120 --> 00:29:25.480
I have to tell you something, Angela.
安吉拉，我得告诉你一件事。

716
00:29:25.580 --> 00:29:25.740
What?
什么？

717
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:27.900
My computer on the pilot was real.
我在拍试播集时用的电脑是真的。

718
00:29:28.180 --> 00:29:29.580
Son of a b****, Jenna.
该死的，珍娜。

719
00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:30.100
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

720
00:29:30.420 --> 00:29:31.880
Maincast got real computers.
主演们用的都是真电脑。

721
00:29:32.120 --> 00:29:32.720
Shut up!
闭嘴！

722
00:29:34.920 --> 00:29:38.420
You and John and Rain had actual computers?
你、约翰还有雷恩用的都是真电脑？

723
00:29:39.060 --> 00:29:39.240
Yeah.
是的。

724
00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:41.880
No internet, but you had games for the pilot?
没有网，但你们拍试播集时有游戏玩？

725
00:29:42.040 --> 00:29:42.220
Yeah.
是的。

726
00:29:42.900 --> 00:29:44.120
Will this ever end?
这什么时候才是个头啊？

727
00:29:44.580 --> 00:29:45.880
Will it ever end?
这真的会结束吗？

728
00:29:46.060 --> 00:29:47.220
All these things I'm learning.
我一直在了解这些新情况。

729
00:29:47.620 --> 00:29:52.760
Well, back in accounting, guys, we had a piece of plastic that they made look like a computer.
好吧，伙计们，在会计部，我们用的就是一块被伪装成电脑的塑料板。

730
00:29:52.860 --> 00:29:54.640
You just had to stare at a plastic box.
你只能盯着一个塑料盒子看。

731
00:29:54.640 --> 00:29:57.200
Piece of plastic that did nothing, so we passed notes.
什么功能都没有的塑料板，所以我们只能传纸条。

732
00:29:57.340 --> 00:29:58.260
We passed a bunch of notes.
我们传了很多纸条。

733
00:29:58.260 --> 00:30:01.200
I haven't known when to tell you this because you've told the story before that our computers…
我一直不知道该什么时候告诉你，因为你之前讲过关于我们电脑的故事……

734
00:30:01.200 --> 00:30:02.360
And you have sat silent?
而你一直保持沉默？

735
00:30:02.360 --> 00:30:06.340
I haven't known how to tell you that all along I had a real computer.
我一直不知道该怎么告诉你，其实我一直用的都是真电脑。

736
00:30:06.500 --> 00:30:07.380
Oh, my God.
天哪。

737
00:30:07.380 --> 00:30:09.360
What else is going to come out in this podcast?
在这个播客里还会爆出什么料？

738
00:30:09.360 --> 00:30:10.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

739
00:30:10.600 --> 00:30:11.380
Holy crap.
天呐。

740
00:30:11.780 --> 00:30:14.680
Well, we passed a lot of notes, and I saved those too.
好吧，我们传了很多纸条，我也把那些都留了下来。

741
00:30:14.880 --> 00:30:15.620
Oscar can draw.
奥斯卡很会画画。

742
00:30:15.720 --> 00:30:21.900
He's a really good drawer, and he would draw me and Brian as Kevin and Angela, and I saved them all.
他画画特别好，他会画我和布莱恩扮演凯文和安吉拉的样子，我都留着呢。

743
00:30:21.900 --> 00:30:22.940
So there, Jenna…
所以，珍娜……

744
00:30:22.940 --> 00:30:25.960
That's what you were doing while I was on my actual computer.
这就是当我用着真电脑时你们在做的事。

745
00:30:26.200 --> 00:30:26.780
Well, whatever.
好吧，无所谓了。

746
00:30:26.980 --> 00:30:32.540
The answer to that story is yes, we were very good at solitaire because it's all we had to do for like two years.
那个故事的答案是肯定的，我们非常擅长玩纸牌游戏，因为那是我们两年来唯一能做的事。

747
00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:33.280
It's true.
这是真的。

748
00:30:33.280 --> 00:30:38.260
And we had on-set free-sell competitions, and we would compete with the cast and crew.
我们还在片场举办过空当接龙比赛，和演职人员一起比。

749
00:30:38.500 --> 00:30:41.920
In between scenes, the crew would sit down at a desk, and they would play free-sell.
在拍摄间隙，工作人员会坐在桌前玩空当接龙。

750
00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:45.160
And Kate Flannery held the title for a very long time.
凯特·弗兰纳里保持冠军头衔很长一段时间。

751
00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:46.680
She was really very good.
她真的很棒。

752
00:30:46.900 --> 00:30:47.260
She is a master.
她是位大师。

753
00:30:47.260 --> 00:30:48.580
Phyllis was also very good.
菲利斯也很棒。

754
00:30:49.140 --> 00:30:50.380
Kate is so good, though.
不过凯特真的很厉害。

755
00:30:50.660 --> 00:30:50.900
Yes.
是的。

756
00:30:51.080 --> 00:30:54.980
With the free-sell, the competition was who could do it in the fewest moves.
在自由接龙游戏中，比赛看谁能用最少的步数完成。

757
00:30:55.780 --> 00:30:56.740
And yeah.
没错。

758
00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:58.100
Kate was really good.
凯特真的很厉害。

759
00:30:58.400 --> 00:31:00.100
I never made the top 10.
我从来没进过前十名。

760
00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:01.760
I would also lose patience.
我也会失去耐心。

761
00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:04.760
Okay.
好的。

762
00:31:04.960 --> 00:31:05.260
All right.
行吧。

763
00:31:05.420 --> 00:31:06.080
Get going.
开始吧。

764
00:31:06.240 --> 00:31:07.540
What else you got over there, Fisher?
费舍尔，你那边还有什么？

765
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:10.800
What else are you hiding from me that you're not telling me?
你还有什么瞒着我没告诉我的？

766
00:31:10.940 --> 00:31:12.480
What other perks did you have?
你还有什么其他福利吗？

767
00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:16.300
Well, this wasn't really a perk, but this was a little sneaky.
嗯，这算不上什么福利，但确实有点小猫腻。

768
00:31:16.300 --> 00:31:22.760
So, during this episode, off-camera, there was a whole thing going on, and it involved
在那一集拍摄期间，镜头外发生了一件事，涉及

769
00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:23.580
me and Phyllis.
我和菲利斯。

770
00:31:24.200 --> 00:31:31.420
So, Phyllis and I are from St. Louis, Missouri, and during this time, the Cardinals were in
我和菲利斯都来自密苏里州的圣路易斯，当时红雀队正在

771
00:31:31.420 --> 00:31:32.060
the playoffs.
打季后赛。

772
00:31:32.180 --> 00:31:33.140
I remember this.
我记得这件事。

773
00:31:33.320 --> 00:31:39.000
They ended up in the World Series against the Boston Red Sox, and in between scenes, Phyllis
他们最终打进了世界大赛，对阵波士顿红袜队，在拍摄间隙，菲利斯

774
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:42.780
and I would sneak back to my trailer and watch the Cardinals games.
和我经常偷偷溜回我的房车看红雀队的比赛。

775
00:31:42.980 --> 00:31:43.460
Yes.
是的。

776
00:31:43.460 --> 00:31:47.160
And we were rooting hard for the Cardinals, and it was very difficult for us because
我们当时非常支持红雀队，这对我们来说很难，因为

777
00:31:47.780 --> 00:31:50.300
basically everyone else on the set was from Boston.
片场基本上其他人都是波士顿人。

778
00:31:50.820 --> 00:31:52.640
Steve, BJ, John.
史蒂夫、BJ、约翰。

779
00:31:53.760 --> 00:31:54.360
More people.
还有其他人。

780
00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:54.800
Yeah.
是啊。

781
00:31:54.800 --> 00:31:57.840
Everyone was rooting for the Red Sox except for me and Phyllis, and they're really-
除了我和菲利斯，大家都支持红袜队，他们真的——

782
00:31:57.840 --> 00:31:59.140
I rooted for the Cardinals with you.
我和你一起支持红雀队来着。

783
00:31:59.220 --> 00:32:00.040
Do you remember that?
你记得吗？

784
00:32:00.220 --> 00:32:01.360
You don't remember that?
你不记得了吗？

785
00:32:01.500 --> 00:32:01.780
No.
不记得。

786
00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:02.920
Jenna, I'm-
珍娜，我——

787
00:32:02.920 --> 00:32:03.980
You and I are-
你和我——

788
00:32:03.980 --> 00:32:04.580
Is this the end of our friendship?
这是我们友谊的终点吗？

789
00:32:04.580 --> 00:32:04.980
You know what?
你知道吗？

790
00:32:05.180 --> 00:32:07.760
You and I are going to have a talk after this, lady.
录完这个我们得好好谈谈，这位女士。

791
00:32:08.080 --> 00:32:08.720
Well, I did.
好吧，我确实支持过。

792
00:32:08.840 --> 00:32:10.420
You brought me onto your side.
你把我拉到了你那边。

793
00:32:10.980 --> 00:32:17.440
One of the things I remember so distinctly about that World Series is that at the end of
关于那届世界大赛，我记忆最深刻的一件事是，下班后

794
00:32:17.440 --> 00:32:22.560
work, we would stay, and we would all go into John's trailer, and we would watch the
我们留下来，大家都会去约翰的房车里，一起看

795
00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:22.880
game.
比赛。

796
00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:27.060
Angela, if you were in John's trailer, you were rooting for Boston.
安吉拉，如果你在约翰的房车里，那你肯定是在支持波士顿。

797
00:32:27.320 --> 00:32:27.540
Oh.
噢。

798
00:32:27.640 --> 00:32:29.580
Phyllis and I watched it in my trailer.
菲利斯和我是在我的房车里看的。

799
00:32:30.140 --> 00:32:31.820
Wait, I didn't know that-
等等，我不知道那个——

800
00:32:31.820 --> 00:32:32.880
Wait, you weren't-
等等，你没——

801
00:32:32.880 --> 00:32:33.580
Oh, right.
哦，对。

802
00:32:33.580 --> 00:32:34.700
You didn't go in John's.
你没去约翰那儿。

803
00:32:34.940 --> 00:32:35.340
No.
没去。

804
00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:36.220
Oh.
哦。

805
00:32:36.660 --> 00:32:38.780
We were in Ireland, Phyllis and I.
我和菲利斯当时在爱尔兰。

806
00:32:38.920 --> 00:32:39.740
We were in Ireland.
我们在爱尔兰。

807
00:32:40.200 --> 00:32:42.140
Well, John's trailer was really fun.
嗯，约翰的房车里确实很有趣。

808
00:32:42.320 --> 00:32:43.740
A lot of people were in there, so I think-
里面人很多，所以我认为——

809
00:32:43.740 --> 00:32:44.360
Of course they were.
那是当然。

810
00:32:44.520 --> 00:32:48.020
I think I probably stopped by your trailer and was like, brr, brr.
我想我可能去过你的房车，当时觉得，冷冷清清的。

811
00:32:48.240 --> 00:32:49.280
It's a little sad in here.
这里面有点凄凉。

812
00:32:49.300 --> 00:32:52.300
And I went into the party trailer where everyone was gathered.
然后我就去了大家聚在一起的派对房车。

813
00:32:52.420 --> 00:32:58.060
Well, also, Boston swept the series four to zero, so it was a particularly depressing room.
嗯，还有，波士顿队四比零横扫了系列赛，所以那个房间的气氛特别压抑。

814
00:32:58.060 --> 00:33:01.940
I mean, I remember there being snacks and, like, laughter.
我是说，我记得当时有零食，还有笑声。

815
00:33:02.400 --> 00:33:02.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

816
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.940
Phyllis and I were just in my trailer crying.
